Z||000006||terryk||11-07-2001||05:02 PM||||Yep, falls out if the engine overheats.||||reg||1
Z||000007||jelly2m8||11-07-2001||06:04 PM||||Yes those are Heat tabs, They are designed to melt off when the engine gets hot enough to cause damage. The purpose of them are to indicate overheating, in which if they are missing, your warranty is void.<P> most salvage yards place these on engines for this exact reason. You will also find these on reman / rebuilt engines and cylinder heads.<P> New vehicles do not come with these on the engine.<p>[This message has been edited by jelly2m8 (edited 11-07-2001).]||||reg||1
